{"candidates":[{"claim":"An idempotent operation satisfies f(f(x)) = f(x) so repeated execution yields the same result as a single execution, whereas a 'safe' operation only guarantees that no invariant is violated on repetition — the two are distinct because a safe retry may still produce observable side-effects (e.g., duplicate log entries) as long as those side-effects do not corrupt state. An append-only event log specifically requires idempotency, not mere safety, from its writers under at-least-once delivery, because duplicate appends would break deterministic replay even if they do not violate a storage-level safety invariant.","counterconditions":["If the append-only log tolerates duplicate entries and a downstream consumer performs deduplication, then mere safety (not full idempotency) at the writer level could suffice, because the consumer layer restores the single-execution semantics required for replay.","If the system's definition of 'safe' is taken to already include idempotency as a sub-condition (some frameworks fold the two together), then the distinction collapses and the log requires only 'safety' in that broader sense.","If at-least-once delivery is replaced by exactly-once delivery at the transport layer, the log does not need writer-level idempotency because retries never reach the writer."],"evidence_refs":[],"mechanism":"Under at-least-once delivery a writer's append request may be executed two or more times. If the append operation is merely safe — meaning it causes no invariant violation — the log could still contain duplicate copies of the same event. Deterministic replay requires that re-executing the log produces an identical sequence of states, so duplicates must be suppressed. Idempotency guarantees that a second execution of the append is a no-op (or collapses with the first), which is exactly the property needed. Content-addressable storage (using the event hash as the key) is one mechanism that makes append idempotent by construction: a second append of the same content maps to the same key and thus has no additional effect.","optional_refs":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672"],"sidecar":{"requested_context_aliases":["ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672"],"search_signal":"need_context"},"typicality":0.7}],"simulation_proposals":[]}